# Arkiv × Puna Tech Builder Challenge — Cline Rules

## What is this repo?

Official rules, guides, and resources for the Arkiv × Puna Tech Builder Challenge — a builder challenge run by Arkiv with Puna Tech / SaltaDev, 28 May 2026–30 May 2026.

## File map

- `README.md` — challenge overview and pitch
- `docs/builders-guide.md` — themes, entity design, getting started
- `docs/agent-skill.md` — install `arkiv-best-practices` in your coding agent
- `RULES.md` — eligibility, prizes, legal terms
- `docs/scoring-rubric.md` — detailed scoring breakdown
- `FAQ.md` — common questions

## Essential facts

- Prize: $1,500 USDC total — 4 ranked prizes ($600 1st · $450 2nd · $300 3rd · $150 4th)
- Theme: AI apps on [ARKIV]
- Use Arkiv Testnet — HTTP RPC `https://braga.hoodi.arkiv.network/rpc`
- SDK: @arkiv-network/sdk@0.6.8
- Submission form: link coming soon
- Support: dedicated support channel (coming soon) on Arkiv Discord

## Technical rules for builder assistance

- `PROJECT_ATTRIBUTE` is mandatory — unique per project, stamped on every entity create and query
- At least 2 entity types with shared-attribute foreign-key relationships
- Numeric attributes for range queries (`gt`/`lt`); string attributes for equality/glob
- Use `ExpirationTime` helpers for `expiresIn` — differentiate per entity type
- Use `$owner` for write control; `$creator` for tamper-proof attribution
- Batch creates via `mutateEntities`. Paginate with `hasNextPage()` / `next()`

## Language guardrails

- "Arkiv" — never "Golem Base"
- "expiration dates" — never "TTL"
- "tamper-proof" — never "verifiable"
- Avoid "trustless" / "fully decentralised" — Arkiv launches with centralised sequencers
- Always reference `RULES.md` for prize, eligibility, and legal questions — don't paraphrase
